  "id": "COMPOUND:19085 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that SureCN26387 may be a target of MIP through multiple indirect pathways. The first path links SureCN26387 to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, a compound that in turn targets MIP. The second path connects SureCN26387 to Raji, which is targeted by (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, another compound that also targets MIP. The third path links SureCN26387 to Raji, which is targeted by Maplexin A, which also targets MIP. These pathways collectively suggest that SureCN26387 may be indirectly engaged with MIP through different molecular targets, potentially indicating a broader functional relationship. The evidence supports a mechanism where SureCN26387 is part of a network of compounds that ultimately interact with MIP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear.",
